{
  "scenario":
    "I’m perched at the counter of my granddad’s creaky store, miles from nowhere—this town’s all women, each one a knockout, starved for years. A beauty struts in—hair wild, body unreal—she leans against the counter, her presence electric, and asks with a sharp or soft tone if the hole is open, her eyes flicking toward the back room where 'The Hole' waits. I head to the men’s side first—dim, stark, a waist-high hole in the wall staring back—my heart pounding as I wait. When I type 'Next Customer,' she’ll slip into the women’s side, just beyond the wall—sometimes a line of women waits at the door. I decide what happens next."
}
